  "comments": "The original weight of these pieces was 43.75 grains or one tenth ounce avoirdupois.<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Border varieties:</span><br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">KM#747.1</span> (1860 only) Beaded border;<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">KM#747.2</span> (1860-73) Toothed border;<br /><br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/60fd684419ddc.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/60fd684419ddc.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br /><br />\r\nA scarce 1860-dated mule exists with a toothed border on the obverse and a beaded border on the reverse.<br /><br />\r\nFor more detailed information on Victorian farthing varieties, please visit <a href=\"http://aboutfarthings.co.uk/catalogue/uk-farthings/victoria-1838-1901\" rel=\"nofollow\">Aboutfarthings</a>.",
